1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,326
Hi, I am Dhrumil Shah, and this video is

2
00:00:02,366 --> 00:00:04,157
about how I extended Mycroft with a

3
00:00:04,197 --> 00:00:06,177
Phase 2 pipeline that stress-tests nine

4
00:00:06,217 --> 00:00:07,914
machine-learning models and three

5
00:00:07,954 --> 00:00:09,792
ensembles on 120 stocks, with purged

6
00:00:09,832 --> 00:00:11,577
walk-forward validation and market

7
00:00:11,617 --> 00:00:12,140
regimes.

8
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:14,737
Can daily price and volume data predict

9
00:00:14,777 --> 00:00:16,624
whether a stock rises over the next five

10
00:00:16,664 --> 00:00:17,352
trading days?

11
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,853
The signal is tiny, so the real

12
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:20,525
challenge is measuring it honestly.

13
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:23,993
Phase 2 builds on Phase 1's 184,138 rows

14
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:25,404
across 120 tickers.

15
00:00:25,444 --> 00:00:27,858
Phase 1's five review agents stay in

16
00:00:27,898 --> 00:00:30,250
place; Phase 2 focuses on the model

17
00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:31,661
layer beneath them.

18
00:00:32,467 --> 00:00:34,919
I added 18 new causal features, such as

19
00:00:34,959 --> 00:00:37,006
60-day momentum, MACD, Bollinger

20
00:00:37,046 --> 00:00:39,556
position, ATR, distance to 52-week highs

21
00:00:39,596 --> 00:00:41,932
and lows, volume trends, and relative

22
00:00:41,972 --> 00:00:43,961
strength. The model now sees 44

23
00:00:44,001 --> 00:00:44,715
features.

24
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:47,472
A MarketRegimeDetector runs KMeans on

25
00:00:47,512 --> 00:00:49,500
market momentum and volatility, fitted

26
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,479
on training dates only, to label each

27
00:00:51,519 --> 00:00:53,313
day bull or bear, with high or low

28
00:00:53,353 --> 00:00:54,037
volatility.

29
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:57,348
Labels are purged and embargoed to block

30
00:00:57,388 --> 00:00:59,670
leakage. Four expanding walk-forward

31
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:02,108
folds handle validation, and the final

32
00:01:02,148 --> 00:01:04,314
27,600 rows, from March 2025, stay

33
00:01:04,354 --> 00:01:05,881
untouched as a holdout.

34
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,298
Nine models compete:

35
00:01:08,338 --> 00:01:10,824
logistic regression, a linear SVM

36
00:01:10,864 --> 00:01:13,827
trained with SGD, Naive Bayes, LDA, KNN,

37
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:16,693
AdaBoost, histogram gradient boosting,

38
00:01:16,733 --> 00:01:18,468
LightGBM, and XGBoost.

39
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:22,278
Across the folds, the linear SVM ranked

40
00:01:22,318 --> 00:01:24,974
first, at a mean ROC-AUC of 0.513.

41
00:01:25,014 --> 00:01:27,103
Every model sits near 0.5:

42
00:01:27,143 --> 00:01:29,019
this is a hard problem.

43
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:31,547
From out-of-fold predictions only, I

44
00:01:31,587 --> 00:01:32,688
built three ensembles:

45
00:01:32,728 --> 00:01:34,529
a soft vote, a skill-weighted average,

46
00:01:34,569 --> 00:01:36,152
and a stacked logistic-regression

47
00:01:36,192 --> 00:01:36,897
meta-learner.

48
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:40,409
With selection fixed in advance, the

49
00:01:40,449 --> 00:01:43,364
linear SVM scored 0.521 on the holdout,

50
00:01:43,404 --> 00:01:46,250
with a 95% bootstrap interval of 0.510

51
00:01:46,290 --> 00:01:49,068
to 0.533. Logistic regression reached

52
00:01:49,108 --> 00:01:52,023
0.5335, but picked after the fact among

53
00:01:52,063 --> 00:01:54,772
twelve, it is optimistically biased.

54
00:01:55,567 --> 00:01:57,712
Calibration cut the selected model's

55
00:01:57,752 --> 00:01:59,952
expected calibration error from about

56
00:01:59,992 --> 00:02:01,974
0.037 to under 0.03, and the ROC,

57
00:02:02,014 --> 00:02:04,378
precision-recall, and reliability curves

58
00:02:04,418 --> 00:02:05,799
show the full picture.

59
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,784
Regime matters:

60
00:02:07,824 --> 00:02:10,362
in the bull, high-volatility regime,

61
00:02:10,402 --> 00:02:12,940
holdout ROC-AUC reached 0.62, but on

62
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:14,616
only 720 observations.

63
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:17,129
In the largest regime, bull and low

64
00:02:17,169 --> 00:02:19,771
volatility, it was 0.497, essentially

65
00:02:19,811 --> 00:02:20,480
random.

66
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,194
Three more views:

67
00:02:22,234 --> 00:02:23,840
new-feature correlations with the

68
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,620
target, probability distributions by

69
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:27,488
outcome, and consensus accuracy as the

70
00:02:27,528 --> 00:02:28,556
top models disagree.

71
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:30,637
The automated verdict:

72
00:02:30,677 --> 00:02:32,854
the confidence interval excludes 0.5, so

73
00:02:32,894 --> 00:02:34,869
there is weak but measurable ranking

74
00:02:34,909 --> 00:02:36,582
signal. Modest, but honest and

75
00:02:36,622 --> 00:02:37,439
reproducible.

76
00:02:38,233 --> 00:02:40,350
Every model, metric, regime label, and

77
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:42,608
figure is saved to disk, so the analysis

78
00:02:42,648 --> 00:02:44,097
can be audited and rerun.

79
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:46,641
This extension of Mycroft shows how

80
00:02:46,681 --> 00:02:48,148
feature engineering, rigorous

81
00:02:48,188 --> 00:02:50,066
validation, ensembles, and calibration

82
00:02:50,106 --> 00:02:51,985
turn raw market data into evidence you

83
00:02:52,025 --> 00:02:53,629
can trust, even when it is weak.

84
00:02:53,669 --> 00:02:54,588
I'm Dhrumil Shah.

85
00:02:54,628 --> 00:02:55,684
Thanks for watching.
